[06/08/26 13:20:54] INFO     Transcription:  The swapping property   base.py:98
                             tells us that the order of terms does             
                             not affect the sum. So 5x plus 3y is              
                             the same as 3y plus 5x. The grouping              
                             property tells us we can regroup terms            
                             freely using brackets. The result stays           
                             unchanged. These two properties let us            
                             move terms around so that like terms              
                             end up next to each other. Once like              
                             terms are next to each other, combining           
                             them becomes easy.                                
